# A .arch.quilt file: arch parsed as a *dynamically registered* quilt
# language (phase 4b). The impl fragment below is not an opaque string here —
# it is a real rust quote, parsed by tree-sitter inside the arch tree. An
# arch host is data — it stages no computation — so expansion (phase 4d) is
# an identity rebuild that writes the plain .arch sibling this file spells:
#   cargo run -p metaarch-expand -- expand examples/hello.arch.quilt
# and the metaarch CLI consumes this file directly (check/generate load
# .arch.quilt through the same registry, deriving the spec from the
# expanded term's coparse).
system hello

service greeter {
  lang rust
  port 8080
  impl get /hello rust↖
    "hello from a parsed quote!\n"
  ↗
}
